Subject: [PATCH] SwiftBuild: use the Linux Swift Testing plugin directory

Swift Testing installs its library macro plugin in
`lib/swift/host/plugins` on non-Darwin hosts so its runtime RPATH can reach
the host Swift libraries. Swift Build unconditionally searches the Darwin
subdirectory `lib/swift/host/plugins/testing`, causing test targets to import
the Testing module but fail every macro lookup with errors such as:

    error: no macro named 'require'
    error: unknown attribute 'Test'

Select the install directory that Swift Testing actually uses on Linux.

Sentinel: NUCLEUS_SWIFT_BUILD_LINUX_TESTING_PLUGIN_PATH

diff --git a/Sources/SWBCore/Settings/Settings.swift b/Sources/SWBCore/Settings/Settings.swift
index 93889c43..cc204491 100644
--- a/Sources/SWBCore/Settings/Settings.swift
+++ b/Sources/SWBCore/Settings/Settings.swift
@@ -4702,2 +4702,6 @@ private class SettingsBuilder: ProjectMatchLookup {
+        #if os(Linux)
+        let testingPluginsPath = "/usr/lib/swift/host/plugins"
+        #else
         let testingPluginsPath = "/usr/lib/swift/host/plugins/testing"
+        #endif
         switch (ToolchainStyle(toolchain)) {
